{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLYWnsL1iNWRHbkwFwHm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #47 as **done**: it goes to `triage:engineer` for planning, and the `engineer` worker will implement it. The decision is in `.ard/47/triage-lead.md`.\n\n**Why it can go ahead now:** the last triage run stopped at needs-human. The worker has no network, so it couldn't fetch the real endoflife.date data or the yq checksums. Since then, commit 13c30f1 added both. The endoflife.date API responses are saved under `internal/roles/testdata/lts/api/`, and `CAPTURE.md` in that directory records the yq v4.54.3 version and its checksums. The worker no longer has to fetch anything. The owner has also answered all nine open questions in the plan.\n\n**What a maintainer should know:**\n- **Alpine name:** endoflife.date calls the Alpine product `alpine-linux`, not `alpine`, which the issue's plan uses. The product table and the tests must use `alpine-linux`.\n- **Tests the worker can't run:** without network or Docker, it can't run the integration-tagged tests or the image test. Someone has to run those by hand before merge.\n- **Human approval:** the change edits merge-protected paths (the root `Dockerfile`, `deploy/` and `CLAUDE.md`), so the pull request will wait for a human to approve it.\n- **Rebase:** the sibling scanner issues edit the same starter lists, so whichever pull request lands second will need a small rebase.\n- **Follow-up:** adding lts to the repository's own `.ard/` directory is a separate change a human has to make.\n\nI didn't add any reviewers by name. eng-review has no `when:` rule in the config, so it runs on every pull request anyway."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":945,"cache_read_input_tokens":26031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":94